From 6ef052be2302663042d4e454e2c90c312d5047e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chromium Extend <noreply@localhost>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:18:25 +0000
Subject: Stop asking the user to sign in to a Google account

Opening the bookmark manager for the first time produced a card with the
multicoloured Chrome logo, "Get all your bookmarks", and a Sign in button. On a
browser built to not be tied to a Google account, that is the wrong thing to
put in front of someone, and it is not something they asked for.

It was not one card. The same promo is built in six places: the bookmark
manager, the new tab page, the feed, recent tabs, history, and the password and
autofill settings. Each one constructs its own SigninPromoCoordinator with its
own delegate and its own strings, so removing them one at a time would have
meant six edits, six chances to miss one, and six things to re-check on every
rebase.

They do have one thing in common. Every one of them asks the coordinator
canShowPromo() before it shows anything, so a single answer covers all six and
there is nothing left to keep in sync. That is the only line changed.

This removes the asking, not the ability. Signing in is still reachable from
settings for anyone who wants it; what is gone is the browser bringing it up
unprompted, with Google branding, in six different places.

Checked on the phone: the bookmark manager now opens straight to the folder
list, and history shows no promo above the entries.
---
 .../signin/signin_promo/SigninPromoCoordinator.java   | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/android/signin/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ui/signin/signin_promo/SigninPromoCoordinator.java b/chrome/browser/ui/android/signin/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ui/signin/signin_promo/SigninPromoCoordinator.java
index 9511704a28..b01acadad0 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/android/signin/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ui/signin/signin_promo/SigninPromoCoordinator.java
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/android/signin/java/src/org/chromium/chrome/browser/ui/signin/signin_promo/SigninPromoCoordinator.java
@@ -157,7 +157,16 @@ public class SigninPromoCoordinator
 
     /** Determines whether the signin promo can be shown. */
     public boolean canShowPromo() {
-        return !sPromoDisabledForTesting && mMediator.canShowPromo();
+        // Bare: never. Every one of these promos is an unprompted invitation to sign in to a
+        // Google account, complete with the Chrome logo, on a browser whose whole point is not
+        // being tied to one. They turned up in the bookmark manager, the new tab page, the feed,
+        // recent tabs, history and the password settings.
+        //
+        // This is the one place worth changing: all six build a SigninPromoCoordinator and all
+        // six ask it this question before showing anything, so one answer covers them and there
+        // is nothing to keep in sync. Signing in is still reachable from settings for anyone who
+        // wants it; what is gone is being asked.
+        return false;
     }
 
     /** Builds a promo view object for the corresponding access point. */
